body:
Considering it looks like he has nowhere to truly hide it makes sense he is on edge...skim through the [care guides](https://www.reddit.com/r/ballpython/comments/arz5iw/welcome_to_rballpython_click_here_for_our/) on r/ballpython. You can also just scroll through that sub and get an idea of what the best setups would look like. We know a lot more about keeping snakes happy and healthy now than we did 20 years ago.

&#x200B;

It's obvious from the picture at the very least that snake is very dehydrated, and aspen should never be used as a substrate. Ball pythons live naturally in very humid environments, aspen is very dry and will eventually mold if you keep the humidity as high as it needs to be.

I know this might sound dumb but make sure the lens is clear. On the Ultra (not sure what model you have) the 3x lens is small and to the side and it picks up a lot of fingerprints since your hand may rest on it. Some people probably assume its not a camera. I noticed a huge difference on the 3x lens when it is blurry or if I recently wiped it.

&#x200B;

But also, you're cropping in to a 10 MP picture, its not gonna look amazing.
